        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Gibraltar, Europa Point, Little Bay, Rosia Road, southern Spain\n- Organizations: British Overseas Territories\n- People: Ibrahim al-Ibrahim, King Fahd bin Abdulaziz al-Saud, Elizabeth II\n- Products: Ibrahim-al-Ibrahim Mosque, Keightley Way, Nun's Well\n\nFacts:\n- Gibraltar is a British overseas territory on a peninsula connected to southern Spain.\n- The British Overseas Territories share the British monarch Elizabeth II as head of state.\n- The Ibrahim-al-Ibrahim Mosque is a mosque at Europa Point in Gibraltar.\n- The Ibrahim-al-Ibrahim Mosque is also known as the King Fahd bin Abdulaziz al-Saud Mosque and the Mosque of the Custodian of the Two Holy Mosques.\n- Keightley Way connects Rosia Road at Little Bay to the Ibrahim-al-Ibrahim Mosque and Nun's Well at Europa Point.",
